  "scope": "**Scope note:** This phase turns Phase 3's read-only browser into a write path: selection, transfer, cancellation, retry, destructive confirmation, and audit review (XFER-01..07, ACCESS-03/04). It is the **last v1 phase** and adds no second design system — every token, spacing value, and typographic role below is inherited unchanged from Phase 2/3's locked contract (`components.json`, `app/globals.css`, `nav-shell.tsx`, `tier-card.tsx`, `tier-switcher.tsx`, `browse-table.tsx`/`browse-row.tsx`). Where this phase's new surfaces need a visual language that has no precedent yet (job progress, job status, the health-driven caution guard), this contract derives it from an *existing* pattern already proven in this codebase (the tier card's hand-rolled progress bar, its three-state icon/color/chrome convention) rather than inventing a new one.\n\n**Almost every visual decision here is pre-populated from `04-CONTEXT.md`**, which is unusually thorough — the table below the Design System section marks each contract row's source. The handful of genuinely open calls (job-status badge treatment, the Copy/Move toggle shape, the docked-tray layout mechanics, the health-driven guard's color) were explicitly delegated to research/planning discretion in CONTEXT.md's own `## Claude's Discretion` section and are resolved here, not re-asked of the user.",
