   {
    "title": "Motion & Reduced-Motion Contract",
    "body": "(Extends Phase 2's contract to this phase's new animated surface — the indeterminate progress bar.)\n\n- **Indeterminate job progress bar (D-18):** a sweeping fill segment translates across the track by default — motion is the entire signal, since no percentage is being claimed. **Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, this must NOT collapse to a fully static bar** — that reconstructs exactly the \"frozen bar, job actually still working\" failure D-18 explicitly rejects. Instead, substitute a slow (~2s cycle) opacity pulse on the same fill segment — still alive, far less motion than a continuous sweep, and distinct from a genuinely stalled/frozen appearance.\n- **Determinate job progress bar:** width transitions on value change (~200ms ease), `motion-reduce:transition-none` snaps instantly under reduced motion — identical to `tier-card.tsx`'s existing capacity-bar rule, since a determinate bar's number is the primary signal and the animation is decorative here.\n- **Retrying icon (`RefreshCw`):** spins by default; under reduced motion, static icon + subtle opacity pulse — identical rule to `connection-indicator.tsx`'s \"Reconnecting…\" treatment, reused rather than re-derived.\n- **Tray expand/collapse:** a short height transition (~150ms), disabled under reduced motion (the panel snaps open/closed).",
    "order": 5
   },
   {
    "title": "Screen-Reader / Live-Region Contract",
    "body": "(Extends Phase 2's contract, which established the \"frequent value = no live region, infrequent meaningful transition = `aria-live='polite'`\" rule this phase's job rows inherit directly.)\n\n- **Job progress bar (`role=\"progressbar\"`, `aria-valuenow`/`aria-valuemin=\"0\"`/`aria-valuemax=\"100\"`, `aria-label=\"{source} to {dest} transfer progress\"`):** **not** wrapped in `aria-live` — D-19 throttles updates to ~1/sec, but that is still far too frequent for a live announcement, matching the capacity bar's own exemption. Omit `aria-valuenow` entirely (not `0`) while indeterminate, for the identical \"0% is a claim, not an absence\" reason `tier-card.tsx` already documents for unknown capacity.\n- **Job status (queued → running → completed/failed/cancelled/interrupted):** wrapped in `aria-live=\"polite\"` per row — this *is* the meaningful, infrequent event, mirroring the tier card's health-line live region exactly.\n- **The auto-retry-paused guard note:** appears/disappears as part of the same `aria-live=\"polite\"` status region, not a second independent live region — one announcement per meaningful change to a job, not two competing ones.\n- **Destructive confirmation dialog:** the `Dialog` primitive's own focus-trap and `aria-labelledby`/`aria-describedby` wiring (base-ui default) suffices; no bespoke ARIA beyond ensuring the safe action (`Cancel`) receives initial focus, per D-07.\n- **Tray collapsed strip:** the summary text (\"2 transfers running\") sits in its own `aria-live=\"polite\"` region — an infrequent, meaningful count change (a job starting, finishing, or being added to the queue), not a per-second tick.",
    "order": 6
   }
