   "prose": "**Already installed (Phases 2/3):** `Card`, `Badge`, `Progress`, `Alert`, `Skeleton`, `Button`, `Tabs`, `Breadcrumb`, `Switch`, `Table` (`frontend/components/ui/`). Reuse these; do not reinstall.\n\n**Note on `Progress`:** installed since Phase 2 but never actually exercised — `tier-card.tsx` hand-rolls its own `role=\"progressbar\"` div (solid `bg-muted` track, `bg-sidebar-primary`/`bg-destructive` fill, `motion-reduce:transition-none`) rather than importing the primitive, because the primitive's stock look (`h-0.5` hairline track, `bg-primary` fill) is a different, thinner visual weight than the dashboard's capacity bars. **This phase's job progress bar reuses `tier-card.tsx`'s hand-rolled construction, not the `Progress` primitive** — one consistent progress-bar visual language across the whole app (dashboard capacity, job transfer). See Layout → Job row anatomy.\n\n**New primitives this phase needs (add only these — Phase 2 D-05's \"install only what's actually used\" discipline applies unchanged):**\n\n| Component | Used for |\n|-----------|----------|\n| `Checkbox` | Row selection in `browse-row.tsx` (D-01), header \"select all\" in the current folder |\n| `Dialog` | The `Send to…` picker, the collision pre-flight prompt (D-06), and the destructive confirmation (D-07/D-23) — one primitive backs all three modal flows |\n| `Input` | The `New folder` name field inside the `Send to…` dialog (D-04) — no primitive currently installed supports free-text entry |\n| `Separator` | Divides the tray's collapsed strip from its expanded list, the queue page's Active/History sections, and the audit page's filter bar from its table |\n\n**Not added:** `Tooltip` (no interaction in this phase needs it — icon-only controls use `aria-label` per the established convention), `Sheet` (the docked tray is a persistent, always-mounted layout element, not a slide-over overlay — see Layout), `Select`/`Combobox` (the audit page's actor filter uses a plain native `<select>` styled to the existing border/background tokens, and its action-type filter reuses the already-installed `Tabs` primitive — both avoid a new dependency for a small closed or short-list filter)."
