   "prose": "Declared values (must be multiples of 4) — unchanged from the project-wide scale already in use in `tier-card.tsx`/`browse-table.tsx`:\n\n**Exceptions:**\n- **44px minimum touch target**, carried forward unchanged from Phases 2/3 — applies here to: every row checkbox, the tray's expand/collapse toggle, the `Cancel`/`Retry` icon-or-text buttons on a job row, the collision/destructive dialogs' action buttons.\n- **Job/audit row height is content-driven, not fixed.** Unlike `browse-row.tsx`'s flat 44px (which exists to make the virtualizer's fixed-size-row math simple over up to 10,000 entries), a job row carries variable-height content — a two-line progress readout, an optional current-filename line, an optional auto-retry-paused note. D-16 states job history stays small (a handful of transfers a day) indefinitely, so **neither the tray's active list nor the `/jobs` page virtualizes** — a plain scrolling flex column is sufficient and correctly sized to real content.\n- **Tray expanded max-height: 320px** (multiple of 4, new declared value). Bounds the tray so it can never eat the whole viewport on a page with many active jobs; the panel scrolls internally past that height. This is the constant that keeps D-14's tray from reintroducing the unbounded-body-height problem `app/layout.tsx`'s `h-full` (03-10 deviation 3) exists to prevent — see Layout → Docked tray."
