   "prose": "**Gap identified (carried forward, unchanged by this revision).** The implementation does **not**\nfollow a discrete 8-point token scale. It uses fluid, purpose-fit `rem` values throughout\n(`0.65rem`, `0.82rem`, `0.85rem`, `1.15rem`, `1.25rem`, `clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem)`, etc.) chosen\nper-component for visual rhythm rather than snapped to a 4px grid. This was a deliberate authoring\nchoice for a typography-led, editorial layout (Sera style) and is consistent with itself, but it is\n**not** the standard GSD 4/8/16/24/32/48/64 contract.\n\n**Retroactive contract (documents actual state; not a redesign):**\n\n**Exceptions (forward guidance for Phase 3/4 additions to this surface):** New spacing decisions in\nlater phases on this same visual surface (roadmap, dashboard, artifact reader) should snap to\n4px-multiple values (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64) wherever a new value is introduced, to begin\nconverging the surface toward the standard scale — but do **not** retroactively rewrite the passing,\nalready-shipped Phase 02 CSS as part of this contract capture. Icon-only touch targets (`icon-sm`\nbutton = 2.25rem/36px, `icon` = 2.5rem/40px) are an accepted exception to any 44px minimum, consistent\nwith a desktop-first local dev tool; no mobile-specific touch-target audit is in scope for Phase 02."
