  "tagline": "Visual and interaction contract for frontend phases. Generated by gsd-ui-researcher, verified by gsd-ui-checker.",
  "scope": "",
  "chapters": [
   {
    "title": "Layout",
    "body": "- **Page container:** max-width 1100px, centered, horizontal padding `lg` (24px) below the `sm` breakpoint (640px), `xl` (32px) at/above it.\n- **Nav shell:** fixed-height (56px) top header. Left: \"Cinedise Portal\" wordmark in `--font-heading`. This phase renders **no nav links** for `/browse` or `/jobs` — those routes don't exist until Phase 3/4, and adding disabled placeholder links now is speculative UI that contradicts D-05's \"don't pre-build for guessed future needs,\" applied here to nav content as well as component installs. The shell's job this phase is only to establish the persistent header structure Phase 3/4 extend, plus host the connection indicator. Right: the connection indicator (see below).\n- **Tier grid:** CSS grid, `grid-cols-1` below `sm` (640px), `grid-cols-2` at/above it — the 2×2 layout D-01 specifies. Gap `lg` (24px) both axes. **Fixed order: stage, vault, archive, cloud** (D-04) — this order is a literal array/DOM order, never a `sort()` by state.\n- **Card internal layout (top to bottom, uniform across all four tiers per D-02):**\n  1. Header row: tier name (`--font-heading`, Heading role) + state icon (top-right)\n  2. Progress bar + percentage (inline, percentage right-aligned, Display role)\n  3. Free/total line (Body role)\n  4. Health line — swaps content per state (see States below) (Body role, color varies by state)\n  5. Freshness stamp — ticking relative age (Label role, `muted-foreground`)",
    "order": 2
   },
   {
    "title": "Motion & Reduced-Motion Contract",
    "body": "(Open, project-specific accessibility item not covered by the closed UI-consideration taxonomy — resolved here per the ui-consideration-probe's own boundary rules.)\n\n- **Connection-indicator \"Reconnecting…\" state:** icon (`RefreshCw`) spins by default. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, replace the spin with a static icon plus a subtle opacity pulse (or no animation at all) — never a continuously rotating element for a user who has opted out of motion.\n- **Progress-bar fill transitions:** capacity-bar width animates on value change by default (a short, e.g. ~200ms, ease transition). Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, disable the width transition — the bar should snap to the new value instantly, not animate.\n- **Ticking freshness stamp (D-20):** text content updates every second (\"updated 4s ago\" → \"updated 5s ago\"); this is a text-content change, not a CSS animation, and is unaffected by the reduced-motion preference — it stays on regardless.",
    "order": 5
   },
   {
    "title": "Screen-Reader / Live-Region Contract",
    "body": "(Open, project-specific accessibility item — this phase is the project's first genuinely live-updating UI surface, so getting this right here sets the pattern Phase 3/4 inherit.)\n\n- **Ticking freshness stamp:** plain text, **not** wrapped in `aria-live`. It changes every second under normal operation — an `aria-live` region here would spam assistive tech with an announcement every second. Visual-only update.\n- **Progress bar:** native `role=\"progressbar\"` with `aria-valuenow`/`aria-valuemin=\"0\"`/`aria-valuemax=\"100\"` and `aria-label=\"{Tier name} capacity\"`. Not wrapped in `aria-live` — capacity changes are frequent and not the meaningful event for a screen-reader user.\n- **Health line (the actually meaningful, infrequent event — a tier transitioning healthy↔degraded↔unreachable):** wrap the health-line text in `aria-live=\"polite\"` per card, so a screen-reader user is told \"Archive: SMART self-test FAILED — 142 pending sectors\" or \"Archive: unreachable — last seen 14:32\" when it changes, without being spammed on every capacity tick.\n- **Connection indicator label** (\"Live\" / \"Reconnecting…\" / \"Offline\"): `aria-live=\"polite\"` — infrequent, meaningful transitions (HEALTH-04-adjacent: while offline, the whole dashboard is going stale, and a screen-reader user needs to know that without a page-level banner existing to announce it visually, per D-09).\n- **Each card:** `role=\"region\"` with `aria-label=\"{Tier name} storage tier\"` — gives 4 navigable landmarks for screen-reader users, standing in for the visual grid structure.\n- **Skeleton / cold-start card:** `aria-busy=\"true\"` on the card container while no data has arrived (D-13); cleared the instant the first real frame lands.",
    "order": 6
   }
  ],
