  "title": "Phase 3 — UI Design Contract",
  "tagline": "Visual and interaction contract for frontend phases. Generated by gsd-ui-researcher, verified by gsd-ui-checker.",
  "scope": "**Read this contract as extension, not replacement.** Phase 2 shipped a complete, hand-authored\ndesign system (custom BEM-ish CSS classes over Tailwind v4 tokens, `@base-ui/react` headless\nprimitives, no shadcn CLI-generated components). Phase 3 adds four new surfaces — a header search\nfield, a search results page, a persistent tree sidebar, and a traceability table — and every one\nof them is specified here in terms of classes, tokens, and patterns that already exist in\n`src/web/styles/globals.css` and `src/web/components/`. Where a genuinely new primitive is needed\n(the search input, the sidebar track) it is named explicitly as new and grounded in the nearest\nexisting analog.",
  "chapters": [
   {
    "title": "Component Inventory",
    "body": "Enumerated by `npx shadcn info` — 0 CLI-installed components — `shadcn@4.19.0` — 2026-09-02.\nEnumerated by `node -p \"Object.keys(require('@base-ui/react/package.json').exports).length\"` — 83 export paths — `@base-ui/react@1.7.0` — 2026-09-02.\n\nBecause no shadcn components are CLI-installed, this table is doubly non-exhaustive: it lists (a)\nthe two hand-built wrappers that exist today and (b) the specific `@base-ui/react` export paths\nmost relevant to Phase 3's four new surfaces, out of 83 available. Reaching for any other\n`@base-ui/react/*` export, or hand-building a third `cva` wrapper following the `Button` pattern,\nis expected — never treat this as a closed list.\n\n| Component | Import path | Notes |\n|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| `Button` | `src/web/components/ui/button.tsx` (wraps `@base-ui/react/button`) | Variants `default/outline/secondary/ghost/destructive/link`, sizes `default/xs/sm/lg/icon/icon-xs/icon-sm/icon-lg`. Reuse as-is for any Phase 3 button (e.g. \"See all results\", filter-clear). No new button variant is needed. |\n| `Popover` | `@base-ui/react/popover`, wrapped pattern in `src/web/components/reference-preview.tsx` | Existing positioner/portal pattern (virtual-anchor `getBoundingClientRect`, `sideOffset={8}`, `positionMethod=\"fixed\"`). The header search dropdown (D-01) should follow this exact positioning approach if built as a custom popover rather than via `Combobox`. |\n| `Combobox` | `@base-ui/react/combobox` | **New for Phase 3, not yet used.** Purpose-built for D-01/D-02's input + listbox + keyboard-nav + no-Enter-required dropdown. Prefer this over hand-rolling `Popover` + a manual `<input>` for the header search field — it is the more direct primitive for the exact interaction D-02 describes. |\n| `Input` / `Field` | `@base-ui/react/input`, `@base-ui/react/field` | Available for the traceability filter field (D-14) if label/description wiring is wanted; a plain styled `<input type=\"search\">` matching the existing minimal-chrome convention (no other form input exists in the codebase yet) is equally acceptable — no established precedent favors one over the other, so this is implementer's choice. |\n| `Collapsible` | `@base-ui/react/collapsible` | Available but **not** the established disclosure pattern — see next row. Do not default to this for the tree. |\n| native `<details>`/`<summary>` | HTML, styled via `.phase-disclosure`, `.history-milestone`, `.artifact-metadata` classes | **This is the established disclosure convention** (three existing uses in `globals.css`/`roadmap-page.tsx`/`artifact-page.tsx`), not `@base-ui/react/collapsible`. Phase 3's tree nodes and any traceability category groups that collapse should follow this native pattern for visual and keyboard consistency with Phase 2. |",
    "order": 1
   }
  ],
