     "**`--sidebar` and its five siblings (`--sidebar-foreground`, `--sidebar-border`, `--sidebar-accent`, `--sidebar-accent-foreground`, `--sidebar-primary`) were defined in Phase 2's `@theme` block but never consumed anywhere in the codebase — D-09's tree navigator is their first real usage.** Use `--sidebar` for the new left column's background, `--sidebar-border` for its right-edge divider (in place of the generic `--border` `.document-outline` uses), `--sidebar-accent`/`--sidebar-accent-foreground` for the hovered/highlighted tree node. Muted/secondary continue to back cards and result-group containers as elsewhere."
