   "prose": "No new hex/oklch values — draws exclusively from the tokens `app/globals.css` already defines under the `b3Dqcuo4na` preset.\n\n**Accent (`--primary`) convention carried forward as-is:** this app's current shipped code already uses `--primary` as its live accent role everywhere (default `Button` fill, active nav/tab indicators, connection-indicator's \"Live\" state, success checks) — `connection-indicator.tsx`'s own comment records that this **supersedes** an earlier, now-stale v1.0 restriction to `--sidebar-primary`, accepting `--primary`'s measured 2.69:1 dark-mode contrast \"to keep the app identical to the preset.\" This phase does not revisit that tradeoff; it inherits it.\n\n**Accent (`--primary`) reserved for — explicitly, never \"all interactive elements\":**\n1. The primary submit button's fill on both forms (\"Sign in\", \"Set new password\") — `Button`'s default variant, unmodified\n2. Nothing else new this phase (no active-tab/indicator dots exist on these two screens)\n\n**Destructive (`--destructive`) reserved for:**\n1. The generic auth-failure `Alert` (wrong username or wrong password — AUTH-05)\n2. The rate-limited `Alert` (429 — AUTH-05/D-16)\n3. `aria-invalid` styling on the username/password inputs when either alert above is showing (both fields together — see Security-Critical Interaction Contract)\n4. Change-password validation errors (mismatch, too-short)\n\n**Explicitly NOT destructive:** the backend-unreachable fail-closed notice on `/login` (D-11) — this is a connectivity fact, not a wrongdoing-flavored error, and must read as neutral (`Alert` default variant), never framed the same as a credential failure (that would visually leak \"something about your credentials is wrong\" when nothing about them has been checked yet)."
